  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_024, acc 0.629) uses multiprofile + avgpool + concat with PCA-2000 and ViT-L. In the single-profile regime, concat (0.535) and weighted (0.532) fusion were nearly identical, but we have no multi-profile weighted-fusion data point. Uncertainty: It is unclear whether the fusion strategy interacts differently with the aggregated multi-profile representations—avgpool pooling may already produce a representation where weighted fusion adds little, or it could further refine the balance between modalities. This experiment (config_025) changes only the fusion from concat to weighted, holding all other hyperparameters at the best-known values. It is the most informative next step because it isolates a single design variable in the regime where performance is highest, completing the 2×2 (profile × fusion) comparison. If weighted ≈ concat, we can confidently rule out fusion as a further lever and redirect budget toward RNA encoder choice (scvi/scgpt) or image encoder (ResNet50). If weighted > concat, we gain an immediate improvement and a new direction to exploit."
}

